  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "GEOMETRIC TRIANGULATIONS OF A FAMILY OF HYPERBOLIC 3-BRAIDS — We construct topological triangulations for complements of (−2, 3, n)-pretzel knots and links with n ≥7.\n\n**GEOMETRIC TRIANGULATIONS OF A FAMILY OF HYPERBOLIC 3-BRAIDS**\n\n*BARBARA NIMERSHIEM*\n\n27 pp, 22 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We construct topological triangulations for complements of (−2, 3, n)-pretzel knots and links with n ≥7. Following a procedure outlined by Futer and Gu´eritaud, we use a theorem of Casson and Rivin to prove the constructed triangulations are geometric. Futer, Kalfagianni, and Purcell have shown (indirectly) that such braids are hyperbolic. The new result here is a direct proof.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; Organization; Acknowledgments; 2 Ideal triangulations; 2.1 Forming a three-stranded full twist; 2.2 A foundational ideal triangulation; 2.3 Adding layers to extend to p=2 and 3; 2.4 An ideal triangulation for any p; 2.5 Equivalence classes of edges in the triang; 3 Angle structures and the Casson-Rivin progra; 3.2 Volumes of angle structures; 3.3 The Casson-Rivin program; 3.4 Symmetries of angle structures; 4 The space of positive angle structures is no; 4.1 The triangulations are veering; 4.2 Coordinates for the space of positive angl; 4.3 A symmetry of the space of angle structure",
      "lang": "en",
